0..77 Comment "/// This source states how derived path operations find an operand path type."
78..156 Comment "/// The operations are the HoTT book\'s inverse and composite (Lemmas 2.1.1 and"
157..191 Comment "/// 2.1.2) and `ap` (Lemma 2.2.1)."
192..195 Comment "///"
196..233 Comment "/// A parameter uses its binder type."
234..285 Comment "/// A call uses the result type of its declaration."
286..366 Comment "/// In a body and in a type alike, none of these operations needs a stated type."
367..370 Comment "///"
371..421 Comment "/// A recursive call uses its own function result."
422..486 Comment "/// `Path.ap` uses the written result of its parameter function."
487..490 Comment "///"
491..529 Comment "/// - see: #423 — `stated`, `thrice`"
530..576 Comment "/// - see: #546 — `mappedOver`, `mappedInto`"
